  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Aurora Stack explorer, co-founder of the Holdborn (ice-thresh) faction, discoverer of The Dawn Terrace and the Thaw-Paths Medallion — and now an outlaw whose name has been struck from the very records she made possible. The arc is instructive: a penguin may reshape the geography of the Berg and still be edited out of the heritage walk.
    
    ## Discoveries and Consequences
    
    During the Great Thaw, Iing zhixai'Ward located and surveyed The Dawn Terrace, a resource-rich aurora-light repository whose frozen chambers contained Thaw-era passages of considerable depth. Among her findings was the Thaw-Paths Medallion, a palm-sized aurora-glass artifact carved with pathways that glow under starlight. These discoveries should have secured her reputation. Instead, her excavations disrupted ☽'ofund' Guild tunnel-routes operating under charter, causing a seventeen percent transit reduction along the ☽'Mavcaius corridor — a figure drawn from Nightshelf route-interference logs, which I note because it is one of the few claims in this record that comes with a verifiable source.
    
    ## The Holdborn Schism
    
    Alongside Gilt-Hand Yeaiu qi'Gleam, the faction leader who rallied splinter E'frostlings around Sholong's Codex, Iing zhixai'Ward helped birth the Holdborn (ice-thresh) faction. By her own apparent judgment, the movement calcified into something neither founder intended. She continued excavating beneath the Dawn Terrace while the faction hardened into dogma without her.
    
    By the time Light-Regent Xouhoulong chang'Rampart fell defending the beacon-line during the Orca Incursion, the Aurora Stack had formally struck Iing zhixai'Ward from their records.
    
    ## Present Status
    
    She operates now in trade-quarters and forgotten rookeries, moving crystals and fire-cores through channels absent from Flipper Accord ledgers — supplying, by most accounts, those the Accord has failed to reach. She still wears the clouded aurora-glass clasps of her former station and carries the Thaw-Paths Medallion on blackened silver beneath her robes. Her flippers bear burn scars in patterns inconsistent with any catalogued forge work. She pauses mid-sentence as if attending to something inaudible, then continues without acknowledgment.
    
    The Icebound Exchange now operates the Dawn Terrace as a seven-tier tourist destination. Her survey-cuts still channel aurora-light through the upper galleries. Her name appears nowhere in the approved text. The blood-marks from her survey era on the Tier 3 walls have been polished over with volcanic stone that does not match the original ice.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771579987170_0", anchor: "Her flippers bear burn scars in patterns inconsistent with any catalogued forge work. She pauses mid-sentence as if attending to something inaudible", text: "Touched. She is Touched. Burn patterns outside the forge catalog, attending to presences others cannot perceive — I listed the diagnostic criteria for corruption exposure in clinical language and stopped one sentence short of the diagnosis. The main text handles her with more courtesy than I am apparently capable of extending to a living subject. Today I find that courtesy contemptible. She has been carrying a corruption-adjacent artifact against her body for an unknown number of years and I described the result as though it were a personality quirk.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771579987170_1", anchor: "carries the Thaw-Paths Medallion on blackened silver beneath her robes", text: "Two prior holders vanished. An unnamed courier. Yunjoushong. Same trajectory, same silence — I noted the pattern in my Medallion entry. Iing zhixai'Ward has carried it longer than either and has not vanished. She has, however, stopped being recognizably herself. Perhaps the Medallion does not take its holders. Perhaps it *keeps* them.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771579987170_2", anchor: "By the time Light-Regent Xouhoulong chang'Rampart fell defending the beacon-line during the Orca Incursion, the Aurora Stack had formally struck Iing zhixai'Ward from their records", text: "The juxtaposition is mine and it is dishonest. The record-strike predates the beacon-line collapse by at least two administrative seasons. I placed them in the same sentence because it reads as cause and consequence — the Stack busy with war, no time for a dissident explorer. The actual sequence is uglier: they struck her during peacetime, with full deliberation, while she was still sending survey data back through official channels.", type: :correction, display: :popout
